    "result": "Perfect! The fix is working correctly. Both files are created as expected:\n\n1. \u2705 `FRAI-SPEC.md` - the Responsible AI specification template\n2. \u2705 `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` - the GitHub Actions workflow\n\n## Summary of the fix\n\nThe bug was in `/private/tmp/100-tricks-runs/d12/without/t1-flag-bug/r1/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` at line 753. The `gate` command handler was using Commander.js's parsed arguments, but since `--ci` is also defined as an option on the root `frai` program, Commander was consuming it there instead of passing it through to the gate subcommand.\n\n**The fix**: Changed the gate action to extract arguments directly from `process.argv` instead of relying on Commander's parsed arguments:\n\n```typescript\nconst gateIndex = process.argv.indexOf('gate');\nconst gateArgs = gateIndex >= 0 ? process.argv.slice(gateIndex + 1) : args ?? [];\nconst result = spawnSync(process.execPath, [gateCli, ...gateArgs], { stdio: 'inherit' });\n```\n\nThis ensures all flags (including `--ci`, `--smart`, etc.) are passed through correctly to the frai-gate CLI, which then properly creates the GitHub Actions workflow file.",
